# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESTRICTED DATA -- backstop patterns, repo-wide. Do not relax these.
#
# This repo uses DHS Program survey microdata obtained under a signed agreement
# that forbids redistributing record-level data, directly or inside any tool or
# dashboard. `origin` is a public repository, so committing it would breach that
# agreement irreversibly -- once pushed, the data is in the history even after
# deletion.
#
# The directory-level patterns (data/raw/, data/interim/) live in
# pipeline/.gitignore now, next to where that data actually lands. The patterns
# below stay here, repo-wide, on purpose: they're the backstop for a restricted
# file landing somewhere other than pipeline/data/.
#
# See CLAUDE.md and pipeline/docs/dhs-data-terms-constraints.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Statistical package formats, wherever they land. Belt and braces: the
# directory-level patterns in pipeline/.gitignore should already cover them,
# but DHS archives keep their own filenames and a file dropped in the wrong
# directory must still be caught.
*.DTA
*.dta
*.SAV
*.sav
*.SAS7BDAT
*.sas7bdat
*.SD2
*.sd2

# The rest of a DHS recode package. These are not the record data themselves --
# .DCT/.DO/.MAP are variable definitions, .FRQ/.FRW are frequency listings -- but
# they are part of the distributed dataset, which the agreement says is not to be
# shared. Inside pipeline/data/raw/ they are already covered; these patterns are
# the backstop for a file that lands somewhere else.
*.DCT
*.dct
*.DO
*.do
*.FRQ
*.frq
*.FRW
*.frw
*.MAP
*.map
*.SPS
*.sps
*.SAS
*.sas

# Extraction leftovers from DHS archives.
*.ZIP
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordinary housekeeping
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
